Modifications made in this fork, relative to the upstream project:

  - The project, CLI command, and npm package were renamed from "portless"
    to "labelhost" so the fork can be installed and run alongside upstream
    portless without colliding. This covers the user state directory
    (~/.labelhost), the launchd label (dev.labelhost.proxy), the systemd
    unit (labelhost.service), the local CA common name and certificate
    filename (labelhost Local CA / labelhost-ca.crt), and the environment
    variable prefix (LABELHOST_*).
  - Configuration gained a per-app "hostnameTemplate" field supporting
    {{name}} and {{worktree}} placeholders.
  - Configuration can be written in Pkl (labelhost.pkl), amending a schema
    shipped in the package (pkl/Labelhost.pkl) so invalid config fails at
    evaluation time.
  - Configuration is read from labelhost.pkl, then labelhost.json, falling
    back to portless.json and to a "labelhost" or "portless" key in
    package.json, so projects already configured for upstream portless keep
    working. PORTLESS_* environment variables are not read.

